{
  "summary": "Overall the app follows the token‑based visual language and the navigation structure matches the primary flow, but several critical usability and accessibility gaps break the spec. The most serious problem is that the date pickers on the Receipt Capture and Mileage screens are not exposed as standard, focusable, fill‑able fields, causing the automated primary‑flow test to fail and rendering the screens inaccessible for keyboard and screen‑reader users. In addition, a number of required states (error banners on Dashboard, loading/disabled visuals on Export, inline field errors on Auth screens) are missing or only partially implemented, and some components use hard‑coded values instead of design tokens (tab active colour, header safe‑area, overlay colour, focus indication). These issues are high‑severity because they either break the primary flow or leave a user without a defined state. Medium‑severity problems include missing safe‑area handling, omitted tab labels, and colour mismatches. Low‑severity concerns are minor token‑usage inconsistencies and lack of visible focus rings for web keyboards.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The date field is rendered only with @react-native-community/datetimepicker, which on web does not expose a text input that can be filled or labelled. Automation cannot locate the \"Date\" field, breaking the primary flow, and screen‑reader users cannot focus or hear the field.",
      "fix": "Wrap the date picker in a labelled TextInput that opens the native picker on press. Give the TextInput a visible label above, an accessibilityLabel linked via nativeID, and ensure its value is programmatically set. Provide a fallback for web (e.g., <input type=\"date\">) so the field can be filled by automation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Same issue as ReceiptCapture: the mileage date input uses a native picker with no accessible label or focusable element, causing the step \"fill field \\\"Date\\\"\" to time‑out and making the screen inaccessible.",
      "fix": "Implement a labelled TextInput that triggers the native date picker on press, with proper accessibilityLabel and nativeID, and ensure it works in the web build as a regular <input type=\"date\">."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Inline field‑error messages and the top‑toast for submission errors defined in DESIGN.md are not present. Without these, the user never sees the exact copy required for validation feedback, leaving the error state unhandled.",
      "fix": "Add a Text component under each TextInput that displays the specific validation error (e.g., \"Enter a valid email address.\") styled with theme.colors.error. Implement a toast/snackbar that shows \"We couldn’t create your account. Please check the fields and try again.\" on server‑side failure."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing inline validation messages and the \"Incorrect email or password.\" toast on login failure, violating the spec’s error‑state requirements.",
      "fix": "Mirror the error handling from SignUpScreen: display inline errors for each field and a top toast with the exact copy when the login request returns a 401."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The API‑error banner (\"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\") and the offline banner (\"You’re offline – data may be outdated.\") are not implemented, leaving those states undefined.",
      "fix": "Create a Banner component that uses theme.colors.error for the API error and a neutral background for the offline banner. Render conditionally based on network status and API error flags, matching the exact copy from DESIGN.md."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header uses a plain View instead of SafeAreaView, so on iOS devices with notches the app may overlap status‑bar content and violates the safe‑area requirement.",
      "fix": "Replace the outer View with SafeAreaView from 'react-native-safe-area-context' and keep existing styles."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom‑tab bar uses primaryVariant (#004C99) for the active tint, while DESIGN.md specifies primary (#0066FF). Also the tab labels are omitted (tabBarLabel: undefined), whereas the spec allows an optional caption.",
      "fix": "Set tabBarActiveTintColor to theme.colors.primary. Add tabBarLabel props (e.g., \"Dashboard\", \"Add Receipt\", etc.) and ensure the caption style uses theme.typography.caption."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Overlay background colour is hard‑coded as 'rgba(0,0,0,0.3)' instead of using a design token.",
      "fix": "Add an overlay colour token (e.g., colors.overlay = 'rgba(0,0,0,0.3)') to theme and reference it in the style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "No visible focus ring for keyboard navigation on web; Pressable only handles pressed state.",
      "fix": "Track focus state (onFocus/onBlur) and apply a style with a 2 px solid theme.colors.primary outline when focused."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Disabled Export buttons do not use the design token colours (disabledBackground and disabled text) – they appear with default dimmed opacity only.",
      "fix": "Update the Pressable style for the disabled state to use theme.colors.disabledBackground for background and theme.colors.disabled for text, matching the token spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Modal.tsx (or wherever permission modal is implemented)",
      "issue": "Permission modal likely uses the native Alert API, which does not follow the component spec (custom modal with title, body, actions, and themed styling).",
      "fix": "Replace native alerts with a custom Modal component that uses the theme tokens for background, radius, and typography, matching the DESIGN.md modal spec."
    }
  ]
}

