{
  "summary": "The UI largely follows the design spec but several critical gaps prevent a seamless, accessible primary flow. The date field on the Receipt Capture screen cannot be filled, breaking the end‑to‑end user journey. A few visual details (active tab colour, focus outlines) diverge from the token‑based design, and several accessibility best‑practices (focus rings, labelled inputs, password show/hide, autocomplete) are missing or incomplete. These issues range from high‑severity flow blockers to low‑severity polish defects.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The date input field is either missing or not labelled as \"Date\", causing the automated flow to time‑out when attempting to fill it. This leaves the receipt creation state unreachable and breaks the primary flow.",
      "fix": "Add a visible `Text` label \"Date\" linked to a `TextInput` (or DatePicker) via `nativeID`. Ensure the component is focusable and has an accessible role. Use the `theme` tokens for sizing and colours, and include a validation error message under the field."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx (and SignUpScreen.tsx)",
      "issue": "Forms do not have explicit `<Text>` labels above inputs, lack `autoComplete` props, and the password field does not provide a show/hide toggle or live rule list. Submit buttons can be pressed while fields are invalid, leading to hidden errors.",
      "fix": "Add visible labels for email and password, link them to inputs using `nativeID`. Add `autoComplete='email'` and `autoComplete='current-password'` / `new-password'`. Implement a trailing eye‑icon button with `accessibilityLabel='Show password'` that toggles `secureTextEntry`. Validate fields on change, display inline error messages, and disable the submit button until all validations pass."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom tab bar uses `theme.colors.primaryVariant` for the active tint and `theme.colors.secondary` for inactive, which does not match the spec (active should be `primary`, inactive `secondary`). This visual deviation may confuse users.",
      "fix": "Update `tabBarActiveTintColor` to `theme.colors.primary` and keep `tabBarInactiveTintColor` as `theme.colors.secondary`. Adjust any related styling to use the correct tokens."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Custom `Pressable` wrapper for tab buttons does not provide a visible focus outline for keyboard/web navigation, violating the focus‑visibility requirement.",
      "fix": "Add a `style` that applies a 2 px solid `theme.colors.primary` outline when `props.accessibilityState.focused` is true (or use `Pressable`'s `android_ripple`/`focusStyle`). Ensure the outline meets the 44 × 44 px touch‑target guidelines."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx (hypothetical)",
      "issue": "Button component definition (not shown) likely contains hard‑coded colours (e.g., `backgroundColor: '#0066FF'`) instead of referencing `theme.colors.primary`. This breaches the token‑only colour rule.",
      "fix": "Refactor button styles to use `theme.colors.primary`, `theme.colors.onPrimary`, `theme.colors.disabledBackground`, etc., and replace any literal colour values with token references."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header background colour uses `theme.colors.surface` instead of the specified `surface` token, but the border colour uses `theme.colors.secondary` directly; acceptable but could be more explicit with token names. No focus ring on the settings button.",
      "fix": "Replace direct colour usage with token names (`theme.colors.surface` already is a token; ensure consistent naming). Add a focus style to the settings `TouchableOpacity` similar to other interactive elements."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Overlay background uses a hard‑coded rgba string `'rgba(0,0,0,0.3)'` instead of a token‑derived colour. Also, the overlay lacks a `role=\"alertdialog\"` for screen‑readers.",
      "fix": "Define a new token for overlay background (e.g., `overlayBackground`) in `theme.ts` and use it here. Add `accessibilityRole=\"alertdialog\"` to the overlay view for proper announcement."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/theme.ts",
      "issue": "Design token `spacing.lg` is used for header padding, but the spec defines `lg` as 16 px; header padding should be 16 px horizontally (correct). However, the max content width of 360 px is not enforced anywhere (no container style limiting width).",
      "fix": "Create a reusable container component that sets `maxWidth: 360` and `alignSelf: 'center'`, and wrap all screen content inside it."
    }
  ]
}

