{
  "summary": "Overall the app follows the visual language of the design system, but several critical mismatches prevent the primary user flow from completing and violate core design specifications. Automated accessibility (axe & Lighthouse) reports are clean, yet the UI lacks key states, proper token usage, and desktop‑specific layout. The most blocking defect is the Date field on the receipt and mileage screens – it is not a standard, focusable TextInput and the test script cannot fill it, halting the flow at step 25. Additional high‑severity gaps include missing label‑above‑field patterns, live password‑rule helper, field‑level error feedback on the Sign‑Up/Sign‑In screens, and the absence of a navigation drawer on Desktop (the bottom tab bar remains visible). Medium‑severity issues involve hard‑coded colors/dimensions (e.g., tab bar background, header height) that bypass the design tokens, and missing focus‑ring styling on generic buttons. Low‑severity concerns cover ARIA roles for modals/banners, missing live‑region attributes on toasts, and incomplete safe‑area handling. Addressing the high‑severity items is required before the product can be considered production‑ready.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Date field is implemented as a native date picker modal which is not a focusable TextInput; test automation cannot locate or fill it, breaking the primary receipt‑creation flow.",
      "fix": "Replace the date picker with a labeled TextInput (e.g., using @react-native-community/datetimepicker in \"spinner\" mode triggered by a button) that has an accessible `accessibilityLabel` and `nativeID`, and provide a visible fallback text input for manual entry. Ensure the label is placed above the input and that the component updates the form state on change."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The mileage date entry suffers the same non‑focusable picker issue, causing the automation step to time‑out when attempting to fill the ‘Date’ field.",
      "fix": "Implement the mileage date entry using the same accessible TextInput pattern as the receipt screen, with a linked label and appropriate `accessibilityLabel`. Provide a platform‑specific date picker that is triggered only after the TextInput receives focus, not replacing the input element."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑Up screen lacks visible labels above the email and password fields, does not display the live password‑rule helper, and does not show field‑level inline error messages; the submit button can be silently disabled when validation fails.",
      "fix": "Add `<Text>` labels above each `<TextInput>` and link them via `nativeID`. Implement the live password‑rule list that updates as the user types. Show inline error `<Text>` directly under each field when validation fails. Ensure the “Create account” button remains enabled but shows an error toast if submission fails; avoid disabling it without a visible reason."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑In screen suffers from missing labels above inputs, missing field‑level error text, and lacks autocomplete hints for email/password fields; password visibility toggle is not provided.",
      "fix": "Add visible labels linked to inputs, enable `autoComplete` props (`email` for email, `password` for password), display inline error messages, and add a trailing eye‑icon button with `accessibilityLabel=\"Show password\"` that toggles the secureTextEntry prop."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Desktop layout does not hide the bottom tab bar nor provide a navigation drawer as specified; the app always shows the tab bar on web, violating the desktop design spec.",
      "fix": "Detect platform (`Platform.OS === 'web'`) and screen width; render a left‑side navigation drawer (e.g., using `createDrawerNavigator`) on desktop and hide the bottom tab bar. Ensure the drawer contains icons + labels and matches the 240 px width spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Tab bar background uses `theme.colors.surface` (#FFFFFF) instead of the required `background` token (#F5F6FA), diverging from the design system.",
      "fix": "Change `tabBarStyle: { backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface, height: 56 }` to `tabBarStyle: { backgroundColor: theme.colors.background, height: theme.spacing.xl }` (or use the appropriate token) and ensure the height respects the 56 px spec via token if available."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header uses hard‑coded dimensions (height 56) and hard‑coded background colors instead of referencing design tokens for spacing and surface colors.",
      "fix": "Replace `height: 56` with `height: theme.spacing.xl` (or a token representing 56 px) and use `backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface` (already correct) but reference the token values for borders (`theme.colors.secondary`). Also use token spacing for `paddingHorizontal` already done, keep consistency."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "PrimaryButton component (not shown) likely uses custom class names or inline styles without tying to the `theme` tokens for background, text color, border radius, and pressed state.",
      "fix": "Refactor PrimaryButton to consume `theme.colors.primary`, `theme.colors.onPrimary`, `theme.radii.md`, and `theme.spacing` for padding. Use the `Pressable` component's `pressed` state to swap to `theme.colors.primaryVariant`. Add a focus style: `outlineWidth: 2, outlineColor: theme.colors.primary` for keyboard navigation."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Overlay background color is hard‑coded as `'rgba(0,0,0,0.3)'` rather than using a design token for overlay surfaces; also the message text does not include a design‑system typography style for caption.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded background with a token such as `backgroundColor: `${theme.colors.background}80`` (80 % opacity) or a dedicated overlay token. Apply `theme.typography.caption` to the message text."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header `SafeAreaView` uses `accessibilityRole=\"header\"` but does not set `accessibilityLabel` describing the app name; screen readers may not announce the title clearly.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLabel=\"FinanceMate header\"` to the SafeAreaView or to the containing View, and ensure the app title `<Text>` has `accessibilityRole=\"heading\"` with `accessibilityLevel={2}`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PermissionModal.tsx",
      "issue": "Permission modal component (not shown) lacks explicit ARIA roles (`alertdialog`) and does not trap focus, which could cause keyboard users to navigate outside the modal.",
      "fix": "Wrap the modal content in a `<Modal>` component with `accessibilityViewIsModal={true}` and `accessibilityRole=\"alertdialog\"`. Ensure focus is set to the first actionable element when the modal opens and returned to the trigger when closed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Toast.tsx",
      "issue": "Toast component does not specify `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"assertive\"` or use `announceForAccessibility` consistently, which may delay screen‑reader announcements.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"assertive\"` to the toast container and call `announceForAccessibility(message)` when the toast is shown."
    }
  ]
}

