{
  "summary": "The UI largely follows the visual spec but several critical and medium‑severity gaps prevent a smooth primary flow and violate key accessibility and design‑token requirements. The most serious blocker is that the Receipt Capture screen’s Date field cannot be located or focused, which stops the flow at step 25. Sign‑Up/Sign‑In forms also lack visible labels and a password show/hide toggle, breaching accessibility best‑practices. In addition, the bottom tab bar uses the wrong background token, the Dashboard empty‑state CTA is missing, loading overlays don’t display the required copy, and a handful of token and focus‑state details are inconsistent. All of these issues need to be fixed before the product can be considered polished.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Date input is not reachable by the test (and likely by screen readers) because it lacks a visible label, an accessibilityLabel, and a nativeID linking it to a label. This leaves the \"Date\" state unhandled and breaks the primary flow when saving a receipt.",
      "fix": "Add a Text label above the Date picker (e.g., \"Date\"), give the picker a nativeID and accessibilityLabel, and ensure the component renders even when the image placeholder is shown. Use the theme.typography.body for the label and theme.colors.secondary for its color."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Email and Password fields only have placeholders; there are no visible labels above the inputs, violating the spec's requirement for labels above fields and reducing accessibility.",
      "fix": "Add Text components as labels (\"Email address\" and \"Password\") positioned above each TextInput, link them via nativeID, and style them with theme.typography.body and theme.colors.onSurface."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Same as Sign‑Up: missing visible labels for Email and Password fields, resulting in inaccessible forms.",
      "fix": "Add visible labels above each input as described for SignUpScreen, ensuring consistent styling and accessibility linking."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field lacks a trailing eye‑icon to toggle visibility and does not provide an accessibilityLabel \"Show password\". This breaches the sign‑up best‑practice and accessibility requirement.",
      "fix": "Add an eye‑icon button to the right of the password TextInput that toggles secureTextEntry. Set accessibilityLabel=\"Show password\" (and \"Hide password\" when toggled) and ensure the button meets the 44×44 px touch‑target."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field also missing show/hide toggle and accessibility label.",
      "fix": "Implement the same eye‑icon toggle as in SignUpScreen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom Tab Bar background uses `theme.colors.surface` (white) instead of the specified `background` token (#F5F6FA). This deviates from the design token usage.",
      "fix": "Change `tabBarStyle: { backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface, height: 56 }` to `backgroundColor: theme.colors.background`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty‑state UI (illustration, text, and primary CTA \"Add first receipt\") is not implemented, so the app shows a blank screen when the user has no data.",
      "fix": "Create an EmptyState component that follows the spec: show the illustration, title \"No data yet\", body copy, and a PrimaryButton labeled \"Add first receipt\" that navigates to the ReceiptCapture tab."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading overlay shows only a spinner without the required message \"Creating account…\".",
      "fix": "Wrap the ActivityIndicator in a LoadingOverlay component that displays the spinner plus a Text element with the exact copy from the spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading overlay missing the required message \"Signing you in…\".",
      "fix": "Add the exact loading text to the overlay as above."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons are not styled using the Primary/Accent button variants from the design system, and they lack the minimum height (48 px) and min‑width (120 px) constraints.",
      "fix": "Replace generic TouchableOpacity buttons with the PrimaryButton component, set `style` to include `height: 48`, `minWidth: 120`, and apply the token‑based colors/radii."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Permission modal text does not match the exact copy required (\"FinanceMate needs camera access to photograph receipts.\") and the fallback UI button label \"Choose from library\" may be missing or mislabeled.",
      "fix": "Update modal component to use the exact copy from DESIGN.md and ensure the fallback button has the label \"Choose from library\" and appropriate accessibilityLabel."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "API error and Offline banners are not implemented, so the user never sees the messages \"Failed to load data. Pull down to retry.\" or \"You’re offline – data may be outdated.\".",
      "fix": "Add banner components that appear based on error or connectivity state, using theme.colors.error and theme.colors.secondary for background and text."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "The overlay does not set a `role=\"alert\"` or `aria-live=\"assertive\"`, which is required for screen‑reader announcement of loading messages.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"alert\"` and `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"assertive\"` to the container View."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Focus ring is implemented with CSS‑style `outline` which is not supported on React‑Native; keyboard focus on web may not be visible.",
      "fix": "Use `borderWidth: 2` and `borderColor: theme.colors.primary` when `focused` prop is true, or use the `Pressable` `style` function to apply a visible focus style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header only respects top safe‑area inset; on devices with a bottom inset (e.g., iPhone X) the tab bar may overlap content.",
      "fix": "Wrap the entire app (Header + TabNavigator) in a SafeAreaView that includes bottom inset handling."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/theme.ts",
      "issue": "Some screens (not shown) use hard‑coded numeric values for spacing, radius, or colors instead of the theme tokens.",
      "fix": "Audit all style objects and replace literals like `12`, `16`, `#0066FF` with `theme.spacing.md`, `theme.spacing.lg`, and `theme.colors.primary` respectively."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Toast.tsx",
      "issue": "Toast component does not use `announceForAccessibility` to broadcast messages to screen readers.",
      "fix": "Import `announceForAccessibility` from 'react-native' and call it with the toast text when the toast appears."
    }
  ]
}

