{
  "summary": "The current build largely follows the spec but has several critical gaps. The primary export flow fails – the Export CSV button cannot be found or activated – which breaks the core user journey. Many screens (Sign‑Up, Sign‑In, Dashboard empty state, Receipt Capture, Mileage Entry) lack required states, live validation, inline error messages, and proper accessibility labels. Design tokens are used inconsistently (e.g., background vs. surface colors, active tab colour) and some components miss required focus indicators. Navigation to primary actions is present, but the header navigation placeholder, safe‑area handling for the tab bar, and proper semantics are incomplete. These issues must be addressed before the app can be considered production‑ready.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export CSV button is not rendered or not accessible – the automation test times out when trying to click it, breaking the primary export flow.",
      "fix": "Implement ExportScreen to render two primary CTA buttons with the exact text \"Export CSV\" and \"Export PDF\". Attach onPress handlers that call the backend `/export/csv` and `/export/pdf` endpoints, display loading spinners, and show success/error toasts. Add `accessibilityRole=\"button\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Export CSV\"` (and PDF) so the test can locate them."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty‑state UI does not include the required primary CTA \"Add first receipt\" and the exact copy \"You haven’t added any receipts or mileage yet. Tap the + button to get started.\" as defined in DESIGN.md.",
      "fix": "Add a conditional render for the empty dashboard state that shows an illustration, the title \"No data yet\", body copy, and a primary button labelled \"Add first receipt\". Ensure the button triggers navigation to the Receipt Capture screen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑Up screen is missing required field‑level error messages, live password rule list, and proper loading overlay with the exact message \"Creating account…\". The submit button can become silently disabled, violating sign‑up best practices.",
      "fix": "Add visible inline Text components under each input that display validation errors (e.g., invalid email, password rules). Show a full‑screen overlay with ActivityIndicator and the message \"Creating account…\" during the async request. Keep the \"Create account\" button enabled until the request completes, then show the spinner inside the button while disabling further interaction."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑In screen does not display field‑level validation errors or a loading overlay with the exact text \"Signing you in…\". Errors are only shown as toasts, which is not per spec.",
      "fix": "Implement inline validation messages under the email and password fields, and a loading overlay that shows the spinner with \"Signing you in…\" while authenticating. Ensure the \"Log in\" button is only disabled during the request."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom Tab Bar uses `theme.colors.surface` for background and `theme.colors.primaryVariant` for the active tint, contrary to the spec which requires `background` for the bar and `primary` for the active tab colour.",
      "fix": "Replace `tabBarStyle: { backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface }` with `backgroundColor: theme.colors.background`. Change `tabBarActiveTintColor` to `theme.colors.primary` and keep `tabBarInactiveTintColor` as `theme.colors.secondary`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header background uses `theme.colors.background` while the spec defines the header background as `surface` (#FFFFFF). This creates a visual inconsistency with the design tokens.",
      "fix": "Update the `header` style to use `backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface` and keep the bottom border colour as `theme.colors.secondary`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Permission handling UI does not follow the exact copy and layout specified for the camera permission modal (title, body text, button labels). Accessibility labels for the modal actions are missing.",
      "fix": "Create a modal component that matches the design token styles (background `surface`, radius `lg`) and includes the title \"Camera access needed\", body \"FinanceMate needs camera access to photograph receipts.\", and two buttons labelled \"Allow\" and \"Deny\" with appropriate `accessibilityRole=\"button\"` and labels."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Mileage entry screen lacks a loading overlay with the exact message \"Saving mileage…\" and does not disable inputs while saving.",
      "fix": "Add a full‑screen overlay with an ActivityIndicator and text \"Saving mileage…\" when the save request is in progress. Disable all form inputs during this state."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Settings icon button has a placeholder handler and does not navigate to a Settings screen.",
      "fix": "Implement navigation to a Settings screen (or remove the icon if Settings are not part of the product) and ensure the button has an `accessibilityLabel=\"Settings\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button component (not shown) may use hard‑coded colors or sizes instead of the design tokens, risking inconsistencies across the app.",
      "fix": "Audit `PrimaryButton` to ensure it uses `theme.colors.primary`, `theme.colors.onPrimary`, `theme.radii.md`, `theme.spacing.lg` for padding, and respects the minimum height (48 px) and min‑width (120 px). Add a visible focus ring using `borderWidth:2, borderColor: theme.colors.primary` on focus."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading overlay component may not expose the required `accessibilityRole=\"alert\"` or appropriate ARIA live region for assistive technologies.",
      "fix": "Wrap the overlay content in a View with `accessibilityRole=\"alert\"` and ensure the spinner message is announced via `aria-live=\"assertive\"` (or React Native equivalent)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Email and password inputs do not have `autoComplete` / `textContentType` properties set for native autofill.",
      "fix": "Add `autoComplete='email'` and `textContentType='emailAddress'` to the email field, and `autoComplete='password'` and `textContentType='password'` to the password field."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field lacks a trailing eye‑icon to toggle visibility and appropriate `accessibilityLabel=\"Show password\"`.",
      "fix": "Add an eye icon button to the password input that toggles `secureTextEntry` and includes `accessibilityLabel=\"Show password\"` (and \"Hide password\" when visible)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom Tab Navigator is not wrapped in a `SafeAreaView`, so on phones with a home‑indicator the tab bar may be obscured.",
      "fix": "Wrap the `AnyTabNavigator` (or `MainTabs` container) in a `SafeAreaView` with `edges={['bottom']}` to respect safe‑area insets."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export buttons do not indicate loading state (spinner) or disable when a request is in progress, contrary to the spec’s loading states.",
      "fix": "When a user taps Export CSV or Export PDF, replace the button label with a spinner, disable both export buttons, and display the appropriate loading toast messages \"Generating CSV…\" / \"Generating PDF…\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The button component does not expose a `disabled` visual style that uses `disabledBackground` and `disabled` text colours from the token set.",
      "fix": "Update the disabled style to use `backgroundColor: theme.colors.disabledBackground` and `color: theme.colors.disabled` according to the design tokens."
    }
  ]
}

