We need to confirm cause.

We have ExportScreen component defined in expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx. It has two PrimaryButton components with title "Export CSV" and "Export PDF". The buttons are PrimaryButton component. PrimaryButton is a Pressable with title, style, loads a spinner when loading. The test tries to locate a button with name "Export CSV". How is it matched? In UI testing, they'd search for accessibility role button with name being the accessible label. PrimaryButton sets accessibilityRole="button", and accessibilityLabel given via props, else uses title. In ExportScreen, the PrimaryButton component is passed title="Export CSV", and accessibilityLabel="Export CSV". So the button should have accessible label "Export CSV". However maybe PrimaryButton incorrectly uses accessibilityLabel? Let's review PrimaryButton. In PrimaryButton component:

```
export default function PrimaryButton({ title, onPress, disabled = false, loading = false, accessibilityLabel }: Props) {
  const isDisabled = disabled || loading;

  return (
    <Pressable
      style={({ pressed }) => [
        styles.button,
        isDisabled && styles.disabled,
        pressed && !isDisabled && styles.pressed,
      ]}
      onPress={() => {
        if (!isDisabled) onPress();
      }}
      disabled={isDisabled}
      accessibilityRole="button"
      accessibilityLabel={accessibilityLabel || title}
      accessibilityState={isDisabled ? { disabled: true } : undefined}
      tabIndex={0}
    >
      {loading ? (
        <ActivityIndicator size="small" color={theme.colors.onPrimary} />
      ) : (
        <Text style={[styles.text, isDisabled && styles.textDisabled]}>{title}</Text>
      )}
    </Pressable>
  );
}
```

Yes, alt label wise.

