{
  "summary": "The UI mostly satisfies the DESIGN.md spec – token‑based colors, spacing, and accessible roles are used, Lighthouse reports 100 % accessibility and 100 % best‑practices, and Axe finds no violations. However the primary user flow is broken: the Export CSV button never fires, causing the end‑to‑end test to time out. In addition, several screens/components lack the required UX details (labels above inputs, live password rule list, show/hide password toggle, focus‑ring styling, and proper loading/error handling) that are mandated by the design spec. These gaps are medium‑severity usability issues, but the Export button failure is a high‑severity blocker that prevents users from completing the core export action.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The “Export CSV” button does not respond to a click – the flow test times out at step 33. The button appears disabled or has no onPress handler, so users cannot generate a CSV export.",
      "fix": "Add an onPress handler that calls the backend `/export/csv` endpoint, display a loading spinner (using the PrimaryButton loading state) while waiting, and enable the button only when online. Ensure the button’s `accessibilityState.disabled` reflects its real state and remove any overlay that blocks touches."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The corresponding “Export PDF” button likely suffers the same issue as the CSV button, though the test only flagged CSV. This would also block the export flow for PDF.",
      "fix": "Implement the same onPress logic for the PDF button, handling loading, success toast, and offline banner per spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑Up fields lack explicit `<Text>` labels positioned above the inputs and are not linked via `nativeID`/`accessibilityLabel`. The password field does not show a “show/hide” eye icon, and live password rule feedback is missing.",
      "fix": "Add visible labels for Email and Password, associate them with TextInput via `nativeID`, implement an eye‑icon button with `accessibilityLabel=\"Show password\"` that toggles secure entry, and render the live rule list that updates as the user types. Display inline validation messages under each field when errors occur."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Similar to Sign‑Up, the Sign‑In screen does not show field‑level error messages nor label‑above‑input layout, and the password field lacks a show/hide toggle.",
      "fix": "Mirror the improvements from Sign‑Up: visible labels, nativeID linking, eye‑icon toggle, and inline error messages that focus the first invalid field on submit."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button component does not explicitly enforce the required min‑width (120 px), height (48 px), border‑radius (`md` = 8 px), and focus‑ring (2 px solid primary) styles. Without these, touch targets could be smaller than the 44 × 44 px spec on some platforms.",
      "fix": "Update the PrimaryButton style to use `theme.radii.md`, `theme.spacing.lg` for height, `theme.spacing.xxl` for min‑width, and add a `focusStyle` that renders a 2 px solid `theme.colors.primary` outline when `focused` (or use `Pressable`'s `onFocus`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header component code is not visible, but the spec requires it to be a `banner` landmark with accessible navigation to the Settings screen. If this role or the settings button’s `accessibilityLabel` is missing, screen‑reader users lose a key navigation point.",
      "fix": "Ensure the Header element has `accessibilityRole=\"banner\"`, includes the app name as an `h2` (styled with `theme.typography.h2`), and the Settings icon button has `accessibilityLabel=\"Settings\"` and is focusable."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/App.tsx",
      "issue": "The custom tab‑bar focus style uses a border, but does not provide the exact 2 px solid primary focus ring specified. On web/keyboard navigation the visual cue may differ from the design token.",
      "fix": "Replace the custom `borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.primary` with a consistent focus ring style (e.g., `outlineWidth: 2, outlineColor: theme.colors.primary, outlineStyle: 'solid'`) and ensure no other border styles clash."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading overlay does not set an explicit `accessibilityRole=\"alert\"` or live region, which could leave screen‑reader users unaware of loading states beyond the spinner.",
      "fix": "Wrap the spinner in a view with `accessibilityLiveRegion=\"polite\"` and `accessibilityRole=\"alert\"`, and include the spinner’s message text (e.g., “Loading…”)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/theme.ts",
      "issue": "Design tokens are imported in App.tsx but not consistently used across all components (e.g., some style objects may hard‑code colors or spacing). This can cause visual drift if tokens change.",
      "fix": "Audit all StyleSheet definitions to replace any literal color/spacing values with references to `theme.colors.*` and `theme.spacing.*`. Use the token variables for border radii, shadow elevation, and typography."
    }
  ]
}

