{
  "summary": "The UI matches the design token palette in the overall navigation, but several critical and medium‑severity gaps break the primary user flow and accessibility expectations. The most serious issue is that the ‘Export CSV’ action is not reachable – the automated end‑to‑end flow timed‑out at the Export screen, meaning users cannot complete the final step of the primary flow. In addition, the authentication screens lack proper visible labels and live validation, loading overlays are missing or inconsistent, and the bottom tab bar hides text labels contrary to the spec. These problems must be fixed before the product can be considered production‑ready.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export CSV button is not rendered or not interactable, causing the primary flow to time out at step 33. The button lacks an accessibilityLabel/testID and is either missing or disabled.",
      "fix": "Add a primary Button component that displays the label “Export CSV”, uses the theme’s primary colors, has accessibilityLabel=\"Export CSV\" (and a testID for automated tests), is enabled when online, and triggers the /export/csv endpoint. Include a loading state that disables both Export buttons and shows a spinner while the server generates the CSV."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export screen does not display the required offline banner when the device is offline, violating the spec and preventing users from understanding why export is unavailable.",
      "fix": "Detect network status (e.g., using NetInfo) and render a banner with the exact message “Cannot export while offline.” styled with the error color token. Ensure the banner appears above the export buttons and is announced to screen readers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Email and password fields lack visible <Text> labels above the inputs; they rely on placeholder text only, which fails the accessibility requirement for labeled controls.",
      "fix": "Add <Text> components for “Email address” and “Password” with nativeID linked to the TextInput via the accessibilityLabel or ‘label’ prop. Ensure autocomplete attributes (email, password) are set and the password field includes a trailing eye‑icon with accessibilityLabel=\"Show password\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑Up screen does not display live password rule feedback or inline validation errors as specified (e.g., missing dynamic rule list).",
      "fix": "Implement a live validation component beneath the password field that shows the rule list and updates as the user types. On submission, display inline error text under each field with the exact messages from the spec and a top toast for submission errors."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading overlay and success/error toasts after uploading a receipt are missing, and the UI does not show the “Uploading receipt…” spinner state.",
      "fix": "Wrap the upload call with a full‑screen LoadingOverlay component that displays the spinner and message “Uploading receipt…”. On success, show a toast with text “Receipt saved.”; on failure, show a toast with “Upload failed. Check your connection and try again.”"
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Mileage entry screen does not provide a disabled state with spinner overlay during save, nor does it display the required success and error toasts.",
      "fix": "When the user taps “Save mileage”, disable all inputs, show an overlay spinner with message “Saving mileage…”, then on success display a toast “Mileage entry saved.” on error display “Failed to save mileage. Please try again.”"
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom tab bar hides text labels (tabBarShowLabel: false), diverging from the spec that requires optional 12‑px caption labels and may reduce discoverability and accessibility.",
      "fix": "Set tabBarShowLabel: true and provide a caption element (fontSize 12, color secondary) for each tab. Ensure the caption meets the min‑touch‑target requirements and that the label is read by screen readers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button component does not render a visible focus ring when keyboard‑focused; the spec mandates a 2‑px solid primary outline.",
      "fix": "Add a focusStyle that applies borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.primary when the button receives focus (e.g., using the onFocus prop or the :focus pseudo‑class on web)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Some components use hard‑coded colors (e.g., '#0066FF') instead of theme tokens, which undermines design consistency.",
      "fix": "Replace all literal color values with references to theme.colors (primary, onPrimary, etc.) and ensure spacing uses theme.spacing values."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Modal.tsx",
      "issue": "Permission modal lacks proper ARIA role=\"dialog\" and focus trapping; screen readers may not announce the modal correctly.",
      "fix": "Wrap modal content in a <View> with accessibilityRole=\"dialog\" and implement focus trap (e.g., using react-native-modal or manually moving focus to the first button on open and restoring on close)."
    }
  ]
}

