{
  "summary": "The FinanceMate UI is close to the design spec and passes automated accessibility checks (axe: 0 violations) and most styling linting (no unmatched styles). Design tokens are used in many places, and the app is mobile‑first with a functional bottom‑tab bar. However, critical functional gaps break the primary user flow: the Export CSV button cannot be located/clicked, and desktop navigation lacks the required left‑hand drawer, causing the flow to stall at the export step. Several required states (loading overlays, inline field errors, offline banner, permission‑denied UI) are missing or only partially implemented, and a handful of components still use hard‑coded values or insufficient touch‑target sizing. These issues must be fixed before the product can be considered polished.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The \"Export CSV\" button is not rendered with the exact label \"Export CSV\" or is not focusable/has no accessibility label, causing the end‑to‑end flow to time out when trying to click it.",
      "fix": "Add two large PrimaryButton components with the texts \"Export CSV\" and \"Export PDF\". Ensure each button has `accessibilityRole=\"button\"` and `accessibilityLabel=\"Export CSV\"`/`\"Export PDF\"`, a testID for e2e, and is placed inside a container that respects the 360 px max‑width token. Disable the buttons and show a spinner with the correct loading messages when the export request is in flight."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "Desktop navigation drawer (required for width ≥1280 px) is missing, so on web the bottom tab bar is hidden but no alternative navigation exists, breaking the primary flow on desktop.",
      "fix": "Implement a responsive DrawerNavigator that appears on desktop screens. Populate it with menu items for Dashboard, Add Receipt, Mileage, Export, and Settings, using the design tokens for spacing, colors, and icons. Hide the bottom tab bar only when the drawer is present."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "backend/app/main.py",
      "issue": "The frontend performs a HEAD request to '/' during startup, but FastAPI defines no root endpoint, resulting in 404 responses that can delay navigation and token checks.",
      "fix": "Add a simple root GET (and allow HEAD) endpoint returning `{ \"status\": \"ok\" }` or redirect to `/health`. Update CORS origins if needed."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑Up missing the loading overlay and disabled state defined in the spec (overlay spinner with \"Creating account…\" and fields should be disabled).",
      "fix": "Introduce a `loading` state tied to the async sign‑up call. When true, render `LoadingOverlay` with the correct message, disable all TextInputs (`editable={false}`) and the \"Create account\" button, and prevent multiple submissions."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑In also lacks the loading overlay, disabled fields, and the \"Signing you in…\" spinner required for the loading state.",
      "fix": "Mirror the Sign‑Up loading implementation: show `LoadingOverlay` with the right message, disable inputs and button during submission."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Field‑level validation errors are shown as toasts only; the spec requires inline error text under each field with the exact messages.",
      "fix": "Add a `<Text>` element under each `TextInput` that displays the validation error when present. Use the design token `color.error` for the text and ensure the message matches the spec exactly."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Same inline error issue as Sign‑Up – field errors appear as generic toasts rather than inline messages.",
      "fix": "Implement inline error text under each input, matching the exact wording from the design spec."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button component lacks visual feedback for the pressed state (reduced elevation, background change) and does not render a focus ring for keyboard navigation on web.",
      "fix": "Add `onPressIn`/`onPressOut` handlers to toggle a `pressed` style that switches background to `primaryVariant` and reduces elevation. Add a `focusVisible` style (2 px solid `primary`) via `:focus-visible` for web."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/TextInput.tsx",
      "issue": "Some TextInput styles use hard‑coded color codes (e.g., `#5F5F5F`) and dimensions instead of the design tokens (`colors.secondary`, `spacing.md`).",
      "fix": "Replace all literal color/dimension values with references to `theme.colors` and `theme.spacing`. Ensure border radius uses `theme.radii.sm` and padding uses `theme.spacing.md`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/App.tsx",
      "issue": "Tab bar button pressable does not guarantee the 44 × 44 px minimum touch target; only the icon (24 px) is wrapped, potentially violating touch‑target guidelines.",
      "fix": "Wrap each icon in a container with `minHeight: 44, minWidth: 44, justifyContent: 'center', alignItems: 'center'`. Add padding as needed to meet the 44 px target."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Offline and API‑error banners are not rendered; the dashboard only shows loading and success states, leaving the empty/offline specs unhandled.",
      "fix": "Add a banner component that appears when `useNetInfo().isConnected` is false (offline) or when the dashboard fetch throws (API error). Use the exact messages from the spec and color token `color.error` for the API error banner."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Permission‑denied fallback UI (\"Choose from library\" button) is not present; only the permission prompt modal is shown.",
      "fix": "When camera permission is denied, render a view with the notice text from the spec and a primary button labeled \"Choose from library\" that opens the image picker library fallback."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing explicit loading overlay that disables inputs and shows \"Saving mileage…\" during the save request.",
      "fix": "Add `LoadingOverlay` with the correct message during the mileage POST request, and set `editable={false}` on all inputs while loading."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header uses a plain `<View>` without semantic `<header>` or `accessibilityRole=\"banner\"`, which can affect screen‑reader navigation.",
      "fix": "Wrap the header content in a component with `accessibilityRole=\"banner\"` (or use `<header>` when rendered on web) and ensure the app name is marked as `accessibilityRole=\"header\"`."
    }
  ]
}

