{
  "summary": "The app scores perfect on automated accessibility (axe 0 violations, Lighthouse 100 % a11y) and the basic navigation flow works, but the primary export step is broken – the \"Export CSV\" button cannot be clicked. This stops users from generating reports, a high‑severity defect. In addition there are several medium‑severity gaps against the design spec (missing live password rule UI, missing autocomplete attributes, missing password show/hide toggle, missing field labels linked to inputs, missing focus outlines) and a handful of low‑severity token‑usage/visual style omissions (button sizing, focus rings on web, missing error banners on Dashboard, missing offline banner on Export). These issues must be fixed before the product can be considered polished.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Export screen does not render an interactive button with the exact label \"Export CSV\" (or the button is disabled). The automated flow timed‑out trying to click it, breaking the primary export flow.",
      "fix": "Add two primary Buttons (using the Button component from the design system) with the exact text \"Export CSV\" and \"Export PDF\". Ensure they are enabled, have a touch target ≥44×44 px, use the primary and accent token colors, include a visible focus ring, and wire onPress to the `/export/csv` and `/export/pdf` endpoints. Verify with an end‑to‑end test that the button is reachable and triggers the native share sheet."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Live password rule list is not displayed under the password field, violating the spec's live‑validation UI.",
      "fix": "Render a helper Text component below the password input that lists the password requirements and updates in real time as the user types. Style it with the `secondary` token color and use the `caption` typography token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Email and password TextInputs lack autocomplete attributes (email, current‑password) and visible labels linked via `nativeID`/`accessibilityLabel`.",
      "fix": "Add `<Text>` labels above each input (e.g., \"Email address\", \"Password\") and link them to the inputs via `nativeID`. Set `autoComplete=\"email\"` on the email field and `autoComplete=\"current-password\"` on the password field."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field does not include a trailing eye‑icon toggle with `accessibilityLabel=\"Show password\"`.",
      "fix": "Add an eye‑icon button inside the password TextInput that toggles secureTextEntry. Provide the required accessibilityLabel and ensure the icon's touch target respects the 44 × 44 px minimum."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "API error and offline banners are not implemented; the design spec requires a banner for \"Failed to load data\" and \"You’re offline\" states.",
      "fix": "Detect API fetch errors and offline status and render a banner component at the top of the screen with the appropriate copy and token‑based colors (`error` for API error, `secondary` on `background` for offline)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Buttons lack a visible focus outline (2 px solid `primary`) for keyboard/web navigation.",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` style (or React Native `onFocus` style) that draws a 2 px solid border using `theme.colors.primary`. Ensure the outline is not hidden by overflow."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button height is 48 px but the min‑width is not enforced (some primary buttons render narrower than 120 px).",
      "fix": "Set a style rule `minWidth: theme.spacing.xxl` (120 px) on the Button component to guarantee the minimum width."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header background uses a hard‑coded hex value instead of the `surface` design token.",
      "fix": "Replace the background style with `backgroundColor: theme.colors.surface` and ensure the bottom border uses the `secondary` token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/theme.ts",
      "issue": "CSS fallback for the web does not reference the design tokens; styles are applied via class names without using the `var(--color-…)` custom properties.",
      "fix": "Update any CSS modules or styled‑components to use the CSS variables (`var(--color-primary)`, `var(--space-md)`, etc.) instead of hard‑coded values."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "When the camera permission is denied the fallback UI does not show the “Choose from library” CTA with the exact copy from the spec.",
      "fix": "Render a button labeled exactly \"Choose from library\" and display the copy \"Camera access denied. You can select a photo from your library.\". Use the accent variant for the button so it matches the design token."
    }
  ]
}

